# Go Backend Rules

## Framework & Library Versions (pin these)
- **Go**: 1.22+
- **Fiber**: `github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2` v2.52+
- **GORM**: `gorm.io/gorm` + `gorm.io/driver/postgres`
- **Wire**: `github.com/google/wire` for DI
- **JWT**: `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5`
- **Validator**: `github.com/go-playground/validator/v10`
- **Redis**: `github.com/redis/go-redis/v9`
- **Migrate**: `github.com/golang-migrate/migrate/v4`
- **Zap**: `go.uber.org/zap` for structured logging
- **Testify**: `github.com/stretchr/testify` for tests

## Project Layout (Clean Architecture)
```
internal/
  domain/           # Pure Go structs — NO framework imports here
    entities/       # Event, User, Booking, TicketType, Message …
    valueobjects/   # BookingStatus, EventStatus, UserRole …
    errors.go       # Domain-specific sentinel errors
  repository/
    interfaces.go   # Repository interfaces (contracts)
    postgres/       # GORM implementations
  service/
    interfaces.go   # Service interfaces
    event_service.go
    booking_service.go
    user_service.go
    recommendation_service.go  # Biased Matrix Factorization
    messaging_service.go
  handler/
    v1/             # /api/v1/...
      event_handler.go
      booking_handler.go
      auth_handler.go
      admin_handler.go
      messaging_handler.go
  middleware/
    auth.go         # JWT validation + role extraction
    ratelimit.go
    logger.go
    cors.go
  dto/              # Request/Response structs (separate from domain)
    request/
    response/
```

## Domain Entities — Style Rules
```go
// GOOD — domain entity, no framework tags in struct itself
type Event struct {
    ID          uuid.UUID
    Title       string
    Status      EventStatus
    Organizer   User
    TicketTypes []TicketType
    Bookings    []Booking
    CreatedAt   time.Time
    UpdatedAt   time.Time
}

// GOOD — GORM model in repository layer, separate from domain
type EventModel struct {
    ID    uuid.UUID `gorm:"type:uuid;primaryKey"`
    Title string    `gorm:"not null;size:255"`
    // ...
}

// BAD — mixing GORM tags directly into domain entity
```

## Handler Rules
```go
// ALWAYS use DTO structs — never bind directly to domain entities
type CreateEventRequest struct {
    Title       string    `json:"title"       validate:"required,min=3,max=255"`
    Description string    `json:"description" validate:"required"`
    StartAt     time.Time `json:"start_at"    validate:"required"`
    // ...
}

// ALWAYS validate before doing anything
func (h *EventHandler) CreateEvent(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    var req dto.CreateEventRequest
    if err := c.BodyParser(&req); err != nil {
        return fiber.NewError(fiber.StatusBadRequest, "invalid request body")
    }
    if err := h.validator.Struct(&req); err != nil {
        return fiber.NewError(fiber.StatusUnprocessableEntity, err.Error())
    }
    // ...
}

// ALWAYS return structured error responses
type ErrorResponse struct {
    Error   string            `json:"error"`
    Details map[string]string `json:"details,omitempty"`
}

// ALWAYS use fiber.NewError for HTTP errors — never panic
```

## Service Layer Rules
- Services MUST NOT import Fiber or any HTTP framework
- Services MUST NOT import GORM directly — only repository interfaces
- Business logic validation lives in the service layer
- Repository calls are wrapped in service transactions where needed
```go
// GOOD
func (s *BookingService) CreateBooking(ctx context.Context, req CreateBookingInput) (*Booking, error) {
    event, err := s.eventRepo.FindByID(ctx, req.EventID)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("booking: find event: %w", err)
    }
    if event.Status != domain.EventStatusPublished {
        return nil, domain.ErrEventNotBookable
    }
    // capacity check, atomic decrement via DB transaction ...
}
```

## Repository Rules
- All DB operations accept `context.Context` as first parameter
- Use `db.WithContext(ctx)` on every GORM call
- Transactions for any multi-table write (booking creation, capacity update)
- Never return GORM-specific errors to service layer — wrap them
```go
func (r *eventRepo) FindByID(ctx context.Context, id uuid.UUID) (*domain.Event, error) {
    var model EventModel
    if err := r.db.WithContext(ctx).First(&model, "id = ?", id).Error; err != nil {
        if errors.Is(err, gorm.ErrRecordNotFound) {
            return nil, domain.ErrNotFound
        }
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("eventRepo.FindByID: %w", err)
    }
    return mapper.EventModelToDomain(&model), nil
}
```

## Error Handling Rules
- Use `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)` for error wrapping
- Define domain sentinel errors in `domain/errors.go`
- Handler maps domain errors → HTTP status codes via a central `errorMapper`
```go
// domain/errors.go
var (
    ErrNotFound          = errors.New("not found")
    ErrUnauthorized      = errors.New("unauthorized")
    ErrEventNotBookable  = errors.New("event is not open for booking")
    ErrCapacityExceeded  = errors.New("requested tickets exceed available capacity")
    ErrUsernameTaken     = errors.New("username already taken")
)
```

## Authentication & Authorization
- JWT middleware extracts claims and sets `c.Locals("user", claims)`
- Role guard is a separate middleware factory:
```go
func RequireRole(roles ...domain.UserRole) fiber.Handler {
    return func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
        claims := c.Locals("user").(*jwt.Claims)
        for _, r := range roles {
            if claims.Role == r { return c.Next() }
        }
        return fiber.ErrForbidden
    }
}
// Usage: app.Post("/events", authMiddleware, RequireRole(domain.RoleOrganizer, domain.RoleAdmin), handler.CreateEvent)
```

## Database Migrations
- All schema changes via numbered SQL migration files: `migrations/000001_init.up.sql`
- Never use `AutoMigrate` in production code — only in tests
- Always write corresponding `.down.sql` files

## Concurrency & Capacity Management
- Booking creation MUST use `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` or atomic `UPDATE ... WHERE available >= requested`
- Use Redis distributed lock (`SETNX` + TTL) for high-contention scenarios
- Optimistic locking with version column as fallback

## Logging
```go
// Always structured, never fmt.Println
logger.Info("booking created",
    zap.String("booking_id", booking.ID.String()),
    zap.String("event_id", req.EventID.String()),
    zap.Int("tickets", req.NumberOfTickets),
)
// Errors always log at Error level with full context
logger.Error("failed to create booking", zap.Error(err), zap.String("user_id", userID))
```

## Testing Rules
- Unit tests for all service methods — mock repositories with interfaces
- Integration tests for handlers using `fiber.Test()`
- Table-driven tests preferred
- Test file naming: `event_service_test.go` next to `event_service.go`
- Use `testify/assert` and `testify/require` (require for fatal assertions)

## XML / JSON Export (Requirement 12)
- XML marshaling uses `encoding/xml` with proper struct tags matching the DTD
- Streaming export for large datasets via `xml.Encoder` / `json.Encoder` — never load all records into memory at once

## Recommendation Engine (Requirement 13)
- Implement in `service/recommendation/` as a self-contained package
- Biased Matrix Factorization: user bias + item bias + latent factors
- Train on startup from dataset; periodically retrain (cron via `robfig/cron`)
- Fallback to popularity-based ranking for cold-start users (no booking history)
- Expose via `GET /api/v1/events/recommended` (authenticated)
